# Git — explicit approval required

**Do not** commit, push, create pull requests, or merge unless the user **explicitly** asks in that conversation (e.g. "commit", "push", "open PR", "create pull request").

## After implement-slice or feature work

1. Implement code in `projects/<name>/` only.
2. Tell the user what changed and **where files live**.
3. Stop. Wait for explicit approval before any git write to remote.

## Allowed without asking

- `git status`, `git diff`, `git log` (read-only)
- Local validation (tests, lint) when implementing

## Not allowed unless user says so

- `git commit`, `git push`, `gh pr create`, force push, amend
